# =============================================================================
# Discs, ROMs, BIOS dumps, memory cards and game binaries — NEVER committed.
# They are large, copyrighted, and must stay outside the repo: the pristine
# master is roms/PS2/Digimon World 4 (USA).iso, the BIOS lives in
# bios/, and memcards/savestates live in pcsx2/.
# These extensions are the enforcement; keep the list complete when adding new tooling.
# =============================================================================
*.iso
*.ISO
*.img
*.IMG
*.bin
*.BIN
*.cue
*.CUE
*.chd
*.CHD
*.cso
*.CSO
*.rom
*.ROM
*.z64
*.n64
*.v64
*.gba
*.nds
*.sfc
*.md0
*.mdf
*.isz
*.nrg
*.cdi

# Game executables / modules
*.elf
*.ELF
*.irx
*.IRX
*.self
*.pelf
*.exe

# BIOS, memory cards, savestates, save files
*.p2s
*.p2s.bak
*.ps2
*.PS2
*.mcd
*.mcr
*.mca
*.nvm
*.xps
*.sav
*.backup

# Directories that only ever hold the above
roms/
ROMs/
bios/
BIOS/
memcards/
*.rep
*.gpr

# =============================================================================
# Python
# =============================================================================
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# =============================================================================
# Permuter harness output. target.o is a copy of game code and target.s is its
# transcription, so neither may be committed (CLAUDE.md, Assets: no binary
# extracts). build_target.sh regenerates both.
# =============================================================================
tools/permuter/*/target.o
tools/permuter/*/target.s
tools/permuter/*/output-*/

# Temporary one-function splits written by tools/units.py while checking a
# translation unit; removed on success, ignored so a killed run cannot commit one.
dw4u_*

# Object files are never game data we want: they are build output (or, in the
# permuter harness, a raw copy of game bytes). Belt-and-braces after one slipped
# into a commit: the extension list below did not cover a stray name like
# target_padded.o.
*.o

# =============================================================================
# Build output — objects rebuilt by `make objs` from asm/ and src/.
# =============================================================================
build/

# The retail split: the game's code as assembly text, generated from your own executable
# by tools/split.py (`make asm`; `make check` and configure.py write it when it is missing
# or stale). Never committed; neither is a function's retail instructions wrapped in an
# `asm` function under src/ (tools/asm_body_gen.py prints one for local study).
/asm/

# =============================================================================
# Local toolchain copies — your wibo, the proprietary mwcps2, the open-source
# m2c and decomp-permuter. `DW4_*` points at these (see README §Prerequisites);
# they are never redistributed here, so they are never committed.
# =============================================================================
local/
local

# =============================================================================
# Local working output — gitignored, never committed.
# =============================================================================
states/
save_states/
save_dumps/
captures/
screenshots/
snapshots/
scratch/
scratch_saves/
local/extracted/
extract/
work/

# Ghidra project DB: binary, ~67 MB, rebuildable via pyghidra-run + scripts/
ghidra-projects/
# The same names are often symlinked to a working copy on disk; git treats a
# symlink as a file, so match the names without the trailing slash too.
roms
bios
pcsx2
memcards
ghidra-projects
sstates

# =============================================================================
# Local env and secrets
# =============================================================================
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.ppk

# Standalone mods and unrelated workspace projects belong outside this repo.
/mods/
/extras/

# Host/editor metadata and native presentation output.
.idea/
.agents/
.serena/
/port/frame_*.png
*.afs
*.AFS
*.sfd
*.SFD
*.adx
*.ADX
*.gs
*.gs.zst

# Retired shared-tool folder: use scripts/, testing/ and port/tools/.
/dw4-tools/

# Retired top-level topic folders; use their owning script/doc/data directories.
/analysis/
/reference/
/porting/

# Generated document exports, reference captures and retired running handoffs.
/docs/**/*.pdf
/port/screenshots/
/todo_temp.txt

# Retail executables, one folder per version (dtk-template convention): private, never committed.
orig/*/*
!orig/*/.gitkeep

# Generated by configure.py (dtk-template workflow).
/build.ninja
/objdiff.json
/.ninja_log
/.ninja_deps
